<title>GERMANY: German Linde sees stronger 96 sales.</title>
<headline>German Linde sees stronger 96 sales.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>German engineering group Linde AG said on Wednesday that it expected its 1996 sales would be show a five percent rise and its profits would also be higher.</p>
<p>The group also reported that its nine month group incoming orders were up 1.8 percent to 6.44 billion marks ($4.2 billion).  </p>
<p>German Linde sees stronger 96 sales =2</p>
<p>The company also reported a 6.8 percent rise in group turnover for the first nine months despite a fall in domestic group sales.</p>
<p>It said the decline in its home market had been compensated by a rise in exports.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
